From 9b897194d2071c387ebf348d6f9550ac77d38d44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 2404_87638649 <87638649+2404_87638649@user.noreply.gitcode.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:33:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] OHOS: C++20 compatibility for the clang15/libc++15
 toolchain

The OHOS SDK ships clang 15 with libc++ 15: no <expected>, no <print>,
no <format>, and _LIBCPP_HAS_NO_INCOMPLETE_RANGES hides the ranges
algorithms and views adaptors. <compare>/operator<=> works fine.
libkscreen 6.7.2 is written against C++23; rewrite the C++23-only
constructs in C++20:

  * SetConfigResult: std::expected<void, QString> becomes a small
    struct with the same observable semantics (has_value/error)
  * ranges::min_element/sort/find_if -> iterator-form algorithms
  * views::filter/drop + ranges::to<QList> -> explicit loop
  * views::zip + std::format in doctor.cpp -> index loop + QString::arg
  * <print> include dropped (unused)
  * CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 23 -> 20
